  "major": "Psychology, Religion, and Consciousness",
  "notes": "M.A./Ph.D. in Psychology, Religion, and Consciousness. The Master of Arts degree is awarded after the first two years of study and successful completion of the comprehensive examinations (PRC 800, 0 units, in Y2 Spring). Students seeking the doctorate engage in a third year of coursework including research courses and development of a concept paper for the dissertation. The fourth and fifth years focus on dissertation writing and research (PRC 980, 15 units; prerequisite PRC 911). The live, online portion of PRC classes takes place twice per week during fall, winter, and spring quarters. There are no courses offered during the summer quarter. Self-Directed Studies (PRC 970, 3 units) requires 30 hours and a reflection paper, pre-approved, and is required for the Ph.D.",
